# Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this React Router v7 project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` v2.0.1 using pnpm
- Added as a dependency in package.json
- Updated pnpm-lock.yaml with the new dependency tree

### 2. Code Integration
**Modified: `src/app/root.tsx`**
- Imported the `Analytics` component from `@vercel/analytics/react`
- Added the `<Analytics />` component to the Layout function in the body tag, after Scripts

The Analytics component was placed in the Layout component which wraps all pages, ensuring analytics tracking is enabled across the entire application.

## Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart), I used the React-specific Analytics component since this project uses React Router v7 in SPA mode. The component is framework-agnostic and works perfectly with React Router.

The Analytics component was placed at the end of the body tag alongside other React Router components (ScrollRestoration, Scripts) to ensure proper initialization order.

## Verification

All verifications passed successfully:
- ✅ TypeScript type checking passed
- ✅ Production build completed successfully
- ✅ All 40 tests passed (4 test suites)
- ✅ No linting errors introduced

## Next Steps

To enable analytics tracking:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Navigate to the Analytics tab in the Vercel dashboard
3. Click "Enable" to activate Web Analytics
4. Analytics will start collecting data on the next deployment

The analytics will track page views automatically. Custom events can be tracked using the `track` function if needed in the future.
